<p class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Rentals</p>
<h1>50cc Motorbike Hanoi: First-time Visitors Passenger Use</h1>
<p>Two people on one rented 50cc is one of the most normal sights in Hanoi and one of the most debated plans among visitors, and both facts are true. For a first-time visitor the question is not really whether the machine can carry two, it is whether a rider who met the city this week should spend that week riding it two-up. The verified rate for a 50cc scooter is 200,000 VND per day, the shop sits at 112 Nguyen Van Cu in Long Bien, and this page answers the two-seat question the way a first visit asks it.</p>
<p>It belongs to the <a href="/hanoi-50cc-motorbike-rental/">50cc motorbike rental hub for Hanoi</a> and follows our <a href="/hanoi-50cc-motorbike-rental/first-time-visitors-route-suitability/">route suitability guide for first-time visitors</a>, because the routes decide the two-up question as much as the riders do. For what a rental costs across the lineup, the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">Hanoi motorbike rental cost overview</a> lists every verified price, and the <a href="/faq/">FAQ</a> answers the counter questions visitors ask most. This page handles the passenger half of the visit.</p>
